-- title:
--   Regular local rings with k-rational residue field are formally smooth
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $S$ be a commutative ring in the same universe which is a regular local ring, equipped with a $k$-algebra structure making $S$ essentially of finite type over $k$ (so $S$ is a localisation of a finitely generated $k$-algebra, in the sense of Mathlib's `Algebra.EssFiniteType`). Assume that the structure map $k \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(S) = S/\mathfrak{m}_S$, obtained by composing $k \to S$ with the residue map, is surjective; that is, the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ is $k$-rational, the residue field of $S$ being generated by the image of $k$. The conclusion is that the algebra $S$ is formally smooth over $k$: for every commutative $k$-algebra $A$ and every nilpotent (indeed, square-zero) ideal $I \subseteq A$, every $k$-algebra homomorphism $S \to A/I$ lifts to a $k$-algebra homomorphism $S \to A$, in the formulation of Mathlib's `Algebra.FormallySmooth`. No separability or perfectness hypothesis on $k$, and no restriction on the dimension of $S$, is imposed.
--
--   This is the statement that a regular $k$-rational point of a scheme essentially of finite type over a field is a smooth point (EGA IV₄ 17.15.1–17.15.2 together with 17.5.3), with rationality of the residue field replacing separability of the residue extension or perfectness of the base field. It is used in the form [`Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_isRegularLocalRing_of_algHom_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span`](thm.html#Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_isRegularLocalRing_of_algHom_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span), where the regular local ring is presented through generators of its maximal ideal.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_FormallySmooth_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_surjective_algebraMap_residueField.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open IsLocalRing

theorem Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_isRegularLocalRing_of_surjective_algebraMap_residueField
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [IsRegularLocalRing S]
    [Algebra k S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S]
    (hk : Function.Surjective (algebraMap k (ResidueField S))) :
    Algebra.FormallySmooth k S := by sorry
